    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** serving as our clear offensive anchors. **Yordan Alvarez** (71.83) benefits from an elite 0.421 xwOBA and a favorable matchup against Jack Leiter, while **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (71.52) provides our highest ceiling in the scarcest category; the combination of a 14% boost from a dynamic platoon split and a slow-delivering opposing pitcher, S. Burke, makes him a primary target for stolen base production. Meanwhile, **Junior Caminero** (65.41) and **Casey Schmitt** (63.92) offer strong starts against Junk and Aaron Civale, respectively. **Casey Schmitt** specifically benefits from an impressive 11% bump tied to the SP skill projection, positioning him as a high-floor cornerstone for today\u2019s lineup.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was leaving **Carson Benge** (49.21) out of the active roster. While his projected score is respectable, he ultimately fell short due to a difficult matchup against Schlittler and a SP skill penalty that suppressed his overall efficiency relative to the starters. We are also monitoring risks with our lineup construction; **Hyeseong Kim**, **Luke Raley**, and **Casey Schmitt** are currently awaiting official confirmation, and we have factored in potential lineup shifts to our daily scoring. **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber** face a challenging outing against B. Ashcraft, where the SP skill deficit (-11%) serves as a significant drag on their output. We are proceeding with caution, as these matchups require our hitters to overcome superior arm talent to maintain our efficiency targets.",
